- Thread class is available in java.lang package
- Methods - getName(), setName(),run(), start(), getId(), sleep(),join(),interrupt(),resume(),stop()
#Daemon Thread
- Daemon thread in java is service provider thread that provides services to user thread
- Daemon thread life cycle depends on another thread
- We can make any thread Daemon Thread
- eg. Garbage collector is example of Daemon thread      	 

#Synchronized thread
- synchronized is a keyword used to ensure that only one thread at a time can execute a critical section of code 
  that accesses shared resources.
- To prevent race conditions and ensure thread safety when multiple threads access shared data simultaneously
- two types for synchronization in java synchronized method and synchronized block 
- method synchronization synchronizeentire method and block synchronize particular block of code